  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 465(b)(6), qualified nonrecourse financing is nonrecourse debt from a qualified lender (such as a bank or government agency) that is secured by real property used in the activity of holding real property. This exception allows real estate investors to include certain nonrecourse debt in their at-risk amounts.
