  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 409A(a)(1)(B), a plan violation causes immediate income inclusion of all vested deferrals, plus a 20% additional tax on the amount included, plus an interest charge calculated from the year the compensation was first deferred. For Mercer, the $300,000 would be immediately included in income with these additional penalties.
Wrong (A): The 10% early distribution penalty applies to qualified retirement plans under Section 72(t), not to NQDC plan violations under Section 409A.
Wrong (B): Section 409A violations carry severe consequences; Congress specifically enacted the 20% penalty and interest charge to deter noncompliance.
Wrong (C): There is no 50% excise tax in the Section 409A penalty framework; the additional tax rate is 20%.$EXPL$
